# Line endings are LF everywhere, including on Windows.
#
# Go source is an LF format: gofmt writes LF and compares bytes, so a checkout
# with core.autocrlf=true makes gofmt -l list every file in the repository.
# Generated files have the same problem twice over, because mizu gen compares
# what it produced with what is on disk and would rewrite all of them on every
# run. Go's own repository does this.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The golden files under gen/testdata are compared byte for byte.
gen/testdata/** -text
gen/configgen/testdata/** -text
